# Clay UI

Follow `docs/design.md`.

- Tokens only, from `client/src/styles/abstracts/tokens.css`. Styles follow the 7-1 pattern under `client/src/styles/`, and `main.scss` is the only entry file. This sheet is the one the preview iframe loads. Do not type a hex, a raw radius, or a new font in a component.
- Numbers use `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`.
- A table column and its header use the same alignment. Strings align left. Numbers align right. Actions (buttons) align center.
- Layout is intrinsic. Use `@container`. Do not use a viewport `@media` breakpoint for layout.
- The only media query is `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)`. It may reduce or remove motion only.
- Hover is a warm-gray surface change and slight elevation, only when the element is actionable.
- Focus uses `--focus-ring` and is visible without relying on color alone.
- A disabled control says why when the reason is not obvious.
- Every status has a text label. A screen stays under 50 lines.
- A select’s down chevron sits inset from the right edge, with a little padding beside it. The label keeps a gap before the chevron and does not run underneath it.
